-- Seed Batch 1 gods & angels lore (missing high-tier Beyonders audit):
-- 45 canon-confirmed Sequence 0-2 figures across the 22 pathways, generated
-- from the canonical TS source (src/lib/lore/npcs.ts), same lore_entries
-- INSERT format as the earlier seed migrations. narratorOnly is a TS-only
-- prompt flag (no column), intentionally not persisted. All entries are epoch
-- 5, pathway-keyed, gated to their own sequence (progressive disclosure).
--
-- Every fact was drafted from and adversarially cross-checked against the wiki
-- corpus. The audit's original 54-name list included 9 figures whose corpus
-- tier contradicts Seq 0-2 and which were therefore held back: 7 "Book One/Two
-- Saint" figures (Floren Sauron, Gandalf, Ma'am Greed, Miss Sloth, Mr. Envy,
-- Mr. Gluttony, Mr. Lust) deferred to Batch 2 (Seq 3-4 saints), and 2 with no
-- corpus-confirmed sequence (Basil — in-text hint Seq 6; Kaslana — rank blank).
--
-- UPSERT: 6 slugs here (npc-bladel, npc-cohinem, npc-kotar, npc-olmer,
-- npc-ouroboros, npc-suah) already exist on prod from the issue #213 canon
-- expansion with a different gating model (pathway null, sequences [4]). A plain
-- INSERT would violate the unique-slug constraint, so this is ON CONFLICT DO
-- UPDATE — overwriting those rows with the pathway-keyed / own-sequence versions
-- and making the seed idempotent / re-runnable.

on conflict (slug) do update set
  title = excluded.title,
  category = excluded.category,
  content = excluded.content,
  pathway = excluded.pathway,
  epoch = excluded.epoch,
  city = excluded.city,
  npcs = excluded.npcs,
  sequences = excluded.sequences,
  tags = excluded.tags,
  token_count = excluded.token_count;
